  "reference": "The pinned GGML OpenVINO translator converts differing arithmetic inputs into F32 and converts the result to the declared output type. DIV always uses F32 on these inputs. The CPU oracle composes the original GGML scalar and packed readers, four F32 operators and Berkeley SoftFloat conversions into 282 reference graphs. Ten additional boundary graphs run the original ordinary dense translator expressions with OpenVINO Model::evaluate from the exact OpenVINO build named in llama.cpp CI. Each boundary graph uses two leaf tensors and equal shapes. Matching wide ADD, SUB and MUL use a distinct native-precision route and are outside this fixture."
